DYNAMIC PORT FORWARD
ssh <user>@<IP address> -D 9050 2>/dev/null
-D 9050: This flag (-D) specifies a dynamic port forwarding configuration for a SOCKS proxy.
9050: This is the port number on the remote server that will be used by the SOCKS proxy which is the port used by the tool proxychains.
You can choose any unused port number here, but commonly used ports for SOCKS proxies are between 1024 and 49151.
ssh -D 9050 <user>@<IP address> 2>/dev/null
